084 lm-head-int8-untie: INT8 copy of the tied Gemma 4 output head

Patch 069 repacks a separate bf16 output head to Marlin W8A16; Gemma 4 ties the head to
the embedding table, so its presets kept a bf16 gemv over the whole vocabulary shard every
decode step (131072 x 5376 = 1.41 GB per rank on the 31B). SGLANG_LM_HEAD_INT8_UNTIE=1
(with SGLANG_LM_HEAD_INT8=1) takes the existing non-tied path on a single PP rank: a real
ParallelLMHead is built, the checkpoint embedding is copied into it and patch 069 repacks
that copy. The embedding lookup stays dense bf16; the cost is the INT8 copy in VRAM
(0.70 GB per rank on the 31B: KV pool 330,994 -> 306,418 tokens, still above 262,144).
Covers both served classes (Gemma4ForConditionalGeneration and the unified class the 12B
loads through). Tripwire, tok/s at 1K / 32K / 262K:
gemma4-31b      60.2 / 55.9 / 39.8 -> 70.9 / 65.1 / 44.3
gemma4          90.4 / 85.9 / 64.4 -> 101.8 / 96.4 / 70.2
gemma4-21b-reap 89.2 / 84.7 / 63.5 -> 102.2 / 96.3 / 70.4
gemma4-12b      118.3 / 106.4 / 64.5 -> 149.7 / 131.6 / 73.4
